THIRD-PARTY SOURCE IN THE REPOSITORY

exit-daemon/third_party/onionmasq holds three crates of Onionmasq (Tor Project, commit
849a8d14d165), licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0; their licence texts are copied unchanged
(LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE) and the changes are the patches in
exit-daemon/third_party/patches (see exit-daemon/SOURCE.md).

exit-daemon/Cargo.lock names 552 Rust packages that are fetched at build time and linked
statically into the `exitd` binary (Arti, aws-lc and others, with a mix of MIT, Apache-2.0,
ISC, OpenSSL-style, MPL-2.0 and similar licences). The aggregated attribution that a shipped
binary needs (for example from `cargo about`) is not generated yet; it must exist, and
`cargo audit` must have been run, before an image carries the daemon.
